# T3 review #1: entering LIVE from a playing STUDIO stops X0X's sequencer and releases the 303
# gates at once, so the output is silent within 50 ms. A 303 A note on every step means a note is
# sounding at (almost) any entry phase; the old code left it hung (seq_advance stopped, so the
# gate never fell). Ten entry phases sweep a whole 16th.
wait 300
# a 303 A line: a note on every step (unaccented: the 1 ms release is the fast one)
turn ALGO 2
tap REC
tapkey w0
tapkey w0
tapkey w0
tapkey w0
tapkey w0
tapkey w0
tapkey w0
tapkey w0
tapkey w0
tapkey w0
tapkey w0
tapkey w0
tapkey w0
tapkey w0
tapkey w0
tapkey w0
tap REC
turn ALGO -2
# only the dry 303: no reverb or delay send
param 5 2 1 0
param 5 2 2 0
# --- entry phase 0 ms ---
tap PLAY
wait 0
press PLAY
wait 700
release PLAY
wait 20
expect mode 1
silence 50 -35
shot live_entry_stop.png
press PLAY
wait 700
release PLAY
wait 20
expect mode 0
# --- entry phase 12 ms ---
tap PLAY
wait 12
press PLAY
wait 700
release PLAY
wait 20
expect mode 1
silence 50 -35
press PLAY
